\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,above] {$3$};
\draw (A)--(D) node[pos=.75,right] {$2$};
\draw (A)--(E) node[midway,left] {$8$};
\draw (E)--(B) node[pos=.7,above left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$7$};
\draw (E)--(C) node[pos=.7,above,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$9$};
\draw (E)--(D) node[midway,left] {$1$};
\draw (B)--(C) node[midway,right] {$6$};
\draw (D)--(C) node[midway,below] {$8$};
\foreach \v/\p in {A/above,B/above,C/right,D/below,E/left} {\fill (\v) circle (2pt); \node[\p] at (\v) {$\v$};}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
Finalise $B(0)$. Assign tentative labels $A(3)$, $E(7)$ and $C(6)$.
Finalise $A(3)$, the smallest tentative label. Assign $D(3+2=5)$. The route to $E$ through $A$ costs $3+8=11$, so retain $E(7)$.
Finalise $D(5)$. Lower $E$ to $5+1=6$, recording $D$ as its predecessor. The route to $C$ through $D$ costs $5+8=13$, so retain $C(6)$.
The smallest tentative labels are tied at $6$. Choose $E$ first and finalise it. Its route to $C$ costs $6+9=15$, so retain $C(6)$. Finalise $C(6)$ and stop.
The diagram shows final cumulative labels from $B$ inside the circles. The bold edge is the shortest path.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},x=13mm,y=13mm]
\coordinate (A) at (1,3); \coordinate (B) at (3,2.6); \coordinate (C) at (3.6,1.1); \coordinate (D) at (0.7,0); \coordinate (E) at (0,1.4);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,above] {$3$};
\draw (A)--(D) node[pos=.75,right] {$2$};
\draw (A)--(E) node[midway,left] {$8$};
\draw (E)--(B) node[pos=.7,above left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$7$};
\draw (E)--(C) node[pos=.7,above,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$9$};
\draw (E)--(D) node[midway,left] {$1$};
\draw[line width=1.4pt] (B)--(C) node[midway,right] {$6$};
\draw (D)--(C) node[midway,below] {$8$};
\foreach \v/\d/\p in {A/3/above,B/0/above,C/6/right,D/5/below,E/6/left} {\node[circle,draw=black,fill=white,minimum size=7mm,inner sep=0pt] at (\v) {$\d$}; \node[\p=4mm] at (\v) {$\v$};}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Backtracking from $C$ gives predecessor $B$. The shortest path is $B\text{–}C$, with total weight $6$.
The label at $E$ is $6$ because $B\text{–}A\text{–}D\text{–}E$ costs $3+2+1=6$, less than the direct edge weight $7$. A label records cumulative weight from the start.

Each numerical off-diagonal entry gives one road. Draw each road once.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},x=14mm,y=14mm]
\coordinate (A) at (0,1.5); \coordinate (B) at (2,3); \coordinate (C) at (4,1.5); \coordinate (D) at (1,0); \coordinate (E) at (4,0);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,above left] {$24$};
\draw (A)--(C) node[pos=.3,above] {$9$};
\draw (A)--(D) node[midway,left] {$6$};
\draw (B)--(C) node[midway,above right] {$13$};
\draw (B)--(D) node[pos=.3,left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$17$};
\draw (B)--(E) node[pos=.75,right,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$11$};
\draw (C)--(E) node[midway,right] {$26$};
\draw (D)--(E) node[midway,below] {$35$};
\foreach \v/\p in {A/left,B/above,C/right,D/below,E/below} {\fill (\v) circle (2pt); \node[\p] at (\v) {$\v$};}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Finalise $A(0)$ and assign tentative labels $D(6)$, $C(9)$ and $B(24)$.
Finalise $D(6)$: lower $B$ to $6+17=23$ and assign $E(41)$.
Finalise $C(9)$: lower $B$ to $9+13=22$ and lower $E$ to $9+26=35$.
Finalise $B(22)$: lower $E$ to $22+11=33$. Finalise $E(33)$.
Backtrack along $E\leftarrow B\leftarrow C\leftarrow A$.
$\begin{aligned} \text{Travelling time}&=9+13+11\\&=33\text{ minutes}\end{aligned}$
The shortest route is $A\text{–}C\text{–}B\text{–}E$.

