foundation.solution_text:
1. **Set the start vertex label to 0 and label adjacent vertices tentatively**
Finalise $S(0)$. The first tentative labels are $A(4)$ and $B(7)$; empty circles have no finite label yet.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (S) at (0,1.2);
\coordinate (A) at (2,2.2);
\coordinate (B) at (2,0.2);
\coordinate (C) at (4,2.2);
\coordinate (D) at (4,0.2);
\coordinate (F) at (6,1.2);
\draw (S) -- (A) node[midway, above left, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$4$};
\draw (S) -- (B) node[midway, below left, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$7$};
\draw (A) -- (C) node[midway, above, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$6$};
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$2$};
\draw (B) -- (D) node[midway, below, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$8$};
\draw (C) -- (D) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$3$};
\draw (C) -- (F) node[midway, above right, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$5$};
\draw (D) -- (F) node[midway, below right, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$4$};
\node[circle, draw, fill=white, minimum size=7mm, inner sep=0pt] at (S) {$0$};
\node[left=4mm] at (S) {$S$};
\node[circle, draw, fill=white, minimum size=7mm, inner sep=0pt] at (A) {$4$};
\node[above=4mm] at (A) {$A$};
\node[circle, draw, fill=white, minimum size=7mm, inner sep=0pt] at (B) {$7$};
\node[below=4mm] at (B) {$B$};
\node[circle, draw, fill=white, minimum size=7mm, inner sep=0pt] at (C) {};
\node[above=4mm] at (C) {$C$};
\node[circle, draw, fill=white, minimum size=7mm, inner sep=0pt] at (D) {};
\node[below=4mm] at (D) {$D$};
\node[circle, draw, fill=white, minimum size=7mm, inner sep=0pt] at (F) {};
\node[right=4mm] at (F) {$F$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
2. **Repeatedly select and finalise the smallest tentative label, then update unprocessed neighbours until the destination is finalised**
Select and finalise $A(4)$. Update $B$ from $7$ to $4+2=6$ through $A$, and give $C$ label $4+6=10$. Next finalise $B(6)$ and give $D$ tentative label $6+8=14$. Next finalise $C(10)$, lower $D$ to $10+3=13$, and give $F$ tentative label $10+5=15$. The diagram below shows the labels at $S,A,B,C$ already finalised; $D$ and $F$ are still tentative.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (S) at (0,1.2);
\coordinate (A) at (2,2.2);
\coordinate (B) at (2,0.2);
\coordinate (C) at (4,2.2);
\coordinate (D) at (4,0.2);
\coordinate (F) at (6,1.2);
\draw (S) -- (A) node[midway, above left, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$4$};
\draw (S) -- (B) node[midway, below left, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$7$};
\draw (A) -- (C) node[midway, above, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$6$};
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$2$};
\draw (B) -- (D) node[midway, below, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$8$};
\draw (C) -- (D) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$3$};
\draw (C) -- (F) node[midway, above right, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$5$};
\draw (D) -- (F) node[midway, below right, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$4$};
\node[circle, draw, fill=white, minimum size=7mm, inner sep=0pt] at (S) {$0$};
\node[left=4mm] at (S) {$S$};
\node[circle, draw, fill=white, minimum size=7mm, inner sep=0pt] at (A) {$4$};
\node[above=4mm] at (A) {$A$};
\node[circle, draw, fill=white, minimum size=7mm, inner sep=0pt] at (B) {$6$};
\node[below=4mm] at (B) {$B$};
\node[circle, draw, fill=white, minimum size=7mm, inner sep=0pt] at (C) {$10$};
\node[above=4mm] at (C) {$C$};
\node[circle, draw, fill=white, minimum size=7mm, inner sep=0pt] at (D) {$13$};
\node[below=4mm] at (D) {$D$};
\node[circle, draw, fill=white, minimum size=7mm, inner sep=0pt] at (F) {$15$};
\node[right=4mm] at (F) {$F$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Finalise $D(13)$. Its route to $F$ has weight $13+4=17$, so retain $F(15)$ with predecessor $C$. Now $F$ has the smallest unprocessed label; finalise $F(15)$ and stop.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (S) at (0,1.2);
\coordinate (A) at (2,2.2);
\coordinate (B) at (2,0.2);
